-eb179c8aeabb","position":{"commit_sha":"ea6112a8dd844830ab594a03e24a6607b930cdec","position":"1795234995423749001-fa570824-fa4e-421f-955b-eb179c8aeabb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented on branch f04e-resign, commit f2aadca6429, Gerrit 3470 (hashtag rebar-session-3d705fec). make verify green (21,527 + 226 passed). Unit tests: 9 in tests/unit/test_reclaim_resign.py, including the side-branch era case found by the real-data run. Real-data proof posted on polite-antivirus-bedbug: enforced verify-identity 8,326 -> 0 non-verified, reduced state equal apart from authorship/signature fields. Awaiting LLM-Review and Verified.","timestamp":1795139047678001001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Close evidence (2026-11-20 PST): landed on main as 717c50f8b33 (Gerrit 3470, LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1). On current main 459ad3874dd: tests/unit/test_reclaim_resign.py + test_reclaim_collapse.py 25 passed; check_mechanism_delta.py --check exit 0; check_complexity_baseline.py --check exit 0. make verify green on the change (21,527 + 226, recorded above). Real-data proof counts, per-step durations and the reduced-state comparison are posted on polite-antivirus-bedbug (verify-identity --all enforced: 51418 verified, 0 non-verified, exit 0; 0 disallowed reduced-state paths).","timestamp":1795232561167287001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1795126291911956001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"67394421-9058-4ae3-96b3-9ee8c2cae938","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a274-0dc6-953a-4160"},{"link_uuid":"82f93a23-1b8c-474e-bdfe-c75236ab9089","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8983-a808-7ad5-4d20"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPublishing the reclaimed `tickets` history (epic `polite-antivirus-bedbug`) is held until enforced `verify-identity --all` (`REBAR_IDENTITY_REQUIRE_AUTHENTICATED=1`, no `enforce_since`) passes on the rewritten history. On origin/tickets 37033c41613 it fails 8,379 events: 874 unsigned raw events (253 with no `author_id`), 1,435 raw and 6,070 SNAPSHOT-ledger events signed by keys not on identity `594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d`'s keyring. Operator decision (2026-11-19): re-sign every failing event during the rewrite with the bot key that was on 594c's keyring when it was written, and give the 253 events `author_id` 594c.\n\n## Approach\n\nAn optional re-sign step in the offline collapse engine. All signing happens before the rewrite stream starts; the stream only substitutes bytes.\n\n1. New `src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_resign.py`: `build_resign_plan(shadow, failing, key_files, *, identity_id, boundary) -> ResignPlan`.\n   - `failing` is the array printed by enforced `verify-identity --all --format json` on the same tip (`event_uuid`, `ticket_id`). `key_files` maps keyring public-key text to a public-key file whose private half is held by the ssh-agent at `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`; `ssh-keygen -Y sign -f <public key file>` signs through the agent, so no private key touches disk.\n   - Matching: a uuid naming an active raw event file `<ticket>/<ts>-<uuid>-<TYPE>.json` at the tip is a raw target keyed by its blob id (event files are append-only, so that id names the event throughout history). Otherwise it is looked up in the `authorship_ledger` of active SNAPSHOTs at the tip as a ledger target. A uuid matched by neither raises `ResignError` naming it. The plan records its tip.\n   - Position: raw `{timestamp}-{uuid}` (as `verify_authorship._event_from_file`); ledger `position.position`.\n   - Key choice reuses `attest.authorship.keys_valid_at_anchor` on the ORIGINAL graph, with resolvers scoped to the shadow (`reclaim_collapse._position_commit_map_for_tracker(shadow)`, `authorship.build_ancestry_oracle(shadow)`), anchored at the event's introducing commit. If that commit is an ancestor of the boundary, a key added below the boundary must also satisfy `added_at <= position`, since after the collapse both resolve to the checkpoint and the verifier orders them by position. The supplied passing key with the latest `added_at` is used. None: `ResignError` with the count, before signing.\n   - Pre-flight: each supplied key must be listed by `ssh-add -L`, else `ResignError`. Then every target is signed up front. Raw: set missing `author_id`, sign with `authorship.sign_event_authorship(event, pubfile, principal=identity_id)`, serialize with `canonical_bytes`, check with `authorship.verify_authorship_any_key`. Ledger: `signature` = DSSE over `authorship.build_authorship_statement(event_uuid, content_hash)`, `signer_pubkey` = chosen key. A failed `ssh-keygen` raises `ResignError` naming the target. Plan construction writes no ref or object.\n2. `reclaim_collapse.py`: `collapse_shadow_tracker(..., resign: ResignPlan | None = None)`; `None` keeps today's output byte for byte.\n   - Asserts the branch tip equals the plan's tip.\n   - `_write_base`: the checkpoint AND the ledger-anchor commit (both re-emit the boundary tree via `M 040000 <tree>`) append inline overrides for every boundary-tree path whose blob is a raw target, after the tree line, so the anchor (first parent of all replayed commits) carries signed bytes.\n   - `_diff_lines`: an `M` line whose blob is a raw target becomes an inline override (covers later introductions, `.retired` renames, merges).\n   - `_rewrite_ledger_in_event` re-signs ledger targets after the `commit_sha` re-resolution and counts a re-sign as a change, so a re-sign-only SNAPSHOT is still written. `CollapseResult` gains `events_resigned`, `ledger_entries_resigned`.\n   - Before moving the branch it checks every raw target present at the tip was substituted and every ledger target re-signed; a shortfall raises `ResignError`, deletes the scratch ref, leaves the branch unchanged. `ResignError` is fatal for the run and retryable after fixing the cause.\n3. No CLI flag, config key or env var. The re-sign is a library parameter driven from the publication runbook, like `reclaim_publish.publish_git_ref`. `reclaim_dry_run.py` is unchanged (its equality checks assume a verdict-preserving collapse); the real-data proof uses an out-of-repo driver calling the same functions and timing each step.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_resign.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_collapse.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_reclaim_resign.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nTest-first on synthetic stores under `tmp_path` (style of `tests/unit/test_reclaim_collapse.py`), ed25519 keys made by `ssh-keygen` in `tmp_path`, loaded into an ssh-agent the fixture starts and kills; skipped without `ssh-agent` or ssh-keygen >= 8.9.\n- Happy: identity with KEY_ADD A at ts 1100 and KEY_ADD B at ts 3000 (above the boundary). Targets: unsigned raw at 1500 (below), unsigned raw at 3500, unsigned raw at 3600 without `author_id`, ledger entry at 1200 with `signer_pubkey: null`. After `collapse_shadow_tracker(..., resign=plan, apply=True)` enforced `verify-identity --all` (no `enforce_since`) exits 0; 1500/1200 carry key A and 3500/3600 key B (from the SSHSIG public key); 3600 carries `author_id`.\n- Reduced state equals pre-collapse apart from `authorship` counts and the added `author_id`.\n- Failures, branch left at its tip: target at ts 900 (before A) -> `ResignError` count 1; uuid in neither place -> `ResignError` naming it; key not in the agent -> `ResignError`; plan from another tip refused.\n- Edge: `resign=None` gives the same tip tree as today; empty `failing` changes nothing; a SNAPSHOT carried across commits is signed once (counted via a wrapped signer).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_reclaim_resign.py` passes the happy, failure and edge cases above.\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_reclaim_collapse.py` passes unchanged.\n- [x] `make verify` exits 0.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` exits 0.\n- [x] The Gerrit change is merged with `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.\n- [x] [non-codebase] On a fresh no-remote fetch of current origin/tickets, enforced `verify-identity --all` (no `enforce_since`) on the rewritten history exits 0 with 0 non-verified events; the counts and per-step durations are posted on `polite-antivirus-bedbug`. No production swap is executed.\n  provenance: environment=developer-workstation-scratch-dir; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=simulation — the run fetched the tickets branch by commit into an empty no-remote repo in a scratch workdir and published only to a file:// fake remote inside it\n- [x] [non-codebase] On that same run, reduced state of the rewritten history equals the original apart from `authorship` counts and the added `author_id`s, posted on `polite-antivirus-bedbug`.\n  provenance: environment=developer-workstation-scratch-dir; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=simulation — the run fetched the tickets branch by commit into an empty no-remote repo in a scratch workdir and published only to a file:// fake remote inside it","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_resign.py","reason":"new: ResignPlan builds targets and signs through ssh-agent"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_collapse.py","reason":"optional resign parameter applied in checkpoint, replay and ledger rewrite"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_reclaim_resign.py","reason":"new: happy, failure and edge tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["parent","536b-8930-b922-4063"],["relates_to","8983-a808-7ad5-4d20"],["relates_to","a274-0dc6-953a-4160"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"536b-8930-b922-4063","parent_status_uuid":"afc9f10f-715b-4568-8dda-ebd6284d22ab","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f04e-82d4-e955-4932","ticket_type":"story","title":"Re-sign failing events during the reclaim collapse","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["472c31cf-1725-4c7b-972e-01b9aad91a21","4f82f5da-5ed2-49e3-b274-c6d70c676751","d7748237-fd6a-4798-8535-4c20d400e941","ad9b8f55-6bcb-4ae6-a339-e9f1c9fda7f9","67394421-9058-4ae3-96b3-9ee8c2cae938","0902d1d6-c195-4aa0-8031-6a72244e9d7c","7c226346-a639-4ab8-91d1-36e3196b387c","3d9aa670-d43f-46c0-bd19-3c239a03aa87","025f4b17-6fa6-4bed-980c-e17fb4d2597f","82f93a23-1b8c-474e-bdfe-c75236ab9089","afc9f10f-715b-4568-8dda-ebd6284d22ab","fa570824-fa4e-421f-955b-eb179c8aeabb"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795234995423749002,"uuid":"9b135bbc-efbb-4ba1-a3ea-369609492d1e"}